---
title: "claimTokenAllocation (LegionPreLiquidApprovedSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_supplied: claimTokenAllocation(allocationSig, vestingSig)
    q_check_supplied --> q_check_claimed: tokensSupplied == true
    q_check_supplied --> q_revert_not_supplied: tokens not supplied
    q_check_claimed --> q_verify_alloc_sig: investorPosition[investor].hasSettled == false
    q_check_claimed --> q_revert_claimed: already claimed
    q_verify_alloc_sig --> q_verify_vesting_sig: allocationSig valid from legionSigner (confirms allocation amount)
    q_verify_alloc_sig --> q_revert_alloc_sig: invalid allocation signature
    q_verify_vesting_sig --> q_check_vesting: vestingSig valid from legionSigner (confirms vesting schedule)
    q_verify_vesting_sig --> q_revert_vesting_sig: invalid vesting signature
    q_check_vesting --> q_deploy_vesting: vesting schedule has locked portion
    q_check_vesting --> q_direct_transfer: immediate distribution only
    q_deploy_vesting --> q_transfer_vesting: deploy vesting clone contract
    q_transfer_vesting --> q_mark_settled: askToken.transfer(vestingContract, lockedAmount)
    q_direct_transfer --> q_mark_settled: askToken.transfer(investor, amount)
    q_mark_settled --> q_emit: investorPosition[investor].hasSettled = true, vestingAddress = vestingContract
    q_emit --> [*]: emit TokenAllocationClaimed(investor, amount, vestingContract)
    q_revert_not_supplied --> [*]: revert TokensNotSupplied
    q_revert_claimed --> [*]: revert AlreadyClaimed
    q_revert_alloc_sig --> [*]: revert InvalidAllocationSignature
    q_revert_vesting_sig --> [*]: revert InvalidVestingSignature

    note right of q_verify_alloc_sig
        INV-001: dual signature verification (allocation + vesting) for claim authorization
        INV-002: hasSettled monotonic false->true per investor
        INV-003: no Merkle proof needed; signature-based authorization instead
    end note
